          "short": "not",
          "worked": "For $k\\ne0$, $k(x-a)(x-b)(x-c)=0$ has the same roots as $(x-a)(x-b)(x-c)=0$. Multiplying zero vertical coordinates by $k$ leaves them zero, so the $x$-intercepts are unchanged.",
